      "page_title": "maxmemory: When Eviction Starts",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "When Nothing Can Be Freed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "SET k v",
            "(error) OOM command not allowed when used",
            "memory > 'maxmemory'."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Happens under `noeviction`, or when every key is protected.",
            "Only denyoom / `may-replicate` commands are rejected.",
            "Reads and `DEL` still succeed — you can dig yourself out."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Sizing and Headroom"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Copy-on-write during `BGSAVE` or `BGREWRITEAOF` can double RSS.",
            "On a write-heavy forking instance: `maxmemory` ~50-60% of box RAM.",
            "`maxmemory-clients` (7.0) caps client output buffers separately.",
            "That keeps a slow consumer out of your data budget."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Symptom",
            "Cause",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "high `mem_fragmentation_ratio`",
              "fragmentation",
              "`activedefrag yes`"
            ],
            [
              "`used_memory` at ceiling",
              "too much data",
              "evict or scale"
            ],
            [
              "p99 spikes on evict",
              "big values",
              "`lazyfree-lazy-eviction`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`mem_fragmentation_ratio` = rss / `used_memory`.",
            "Eviction will not help when the real problem is fragmentation.",
            "Eviction is synchronous with commands — it lands in `SLOWLOG`.",
            "Confirm with `LATENCY HISTORY` before blaming the network."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Cluster note",
          "text": "`maxmemory` is per node. An unbalanced slot distribution evicts hot nodes while the rest sit idle."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Read together",
          "items": [
            "`evicted_keys` rate, plus hits and misses.",
            "Rising evictions + falling hit rate = cache too small.",
            "Not misconfigured — just undersized."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "All Eight, Side By Side"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Policy",
            "Scope",
            "Victim"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`noeviction`",
              "none",
              "write fails"
            ],
            [
              "`allkeys-lru`",
              "all keys",
              "least recent"
            ],
            [
              "`allkeys-lfu`",
              "all keys",
              "least frequent"
            ],
            [
              "`allkeys-random`",
              "all keys",
              "uniform random"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "maxmemory: When Eviction Starts (cont.)",
